{"findings":[{"rule_id":"WPS-004","evidence":[{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D12","page":1,"quote":"⌀ 16 H7 (+0.018/0)"},{"kind":"title_block","ref":"surface_treatment","page":1,"quote":"I.Z.B.P. (TRIVALENT)"}],"comment":"The ⌀16 H7 bore carries a tight ISO fit tolerance but the part is zinc plated; plating buildup will reduce the hole diameter and cause assembly interference. The designer must either increase the basic size to allow for coating thickness or add a note requiring the hole to be masked or re-machined after plating."

,
"recommended_correction":"Increase the nominal size of D12 by twice the maximum plating thickness, or add a note specifying masking/re-machining of the bore after I.Z.B.P. plating."}]}
